{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Baskets of holes.</b> Baskets of woven splints, perforated with holes. In our region there are many. And it is the way of pastry-sellers — who are called אובל\"יש בְּלַעַ\"ז — to put them in those baskets."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "the la'az אובל\"יש likely represents Old French oblier or a related form for a type of pastry/wafer-seller"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:50.029468571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}